      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Redundant Move Logic (`libusb_transport.cc`)** In your move constructor for `LibusbTransport`, you correctly use `std::move()` on your `std::unique_ptr`s (`ctx_` and `handle_`). `std::unique_ptr` naturally nulls out the source pointer upon being moved.\n\n* **Improvement:** You only need to reset the primitive members of the `other` object. The smart pointers handle themselves.",
